  "verbalization": "Miconioside A is shown to have a target relationship with Raji, which is then identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and Marsdenoside K. All of these compounds are linked to Carboxylesterase 2, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the enzyme. The evidence implies that Miconioside A may act through a pathway that involves the enzyme Carboxylesterase 2, possibly by targeting a shared downstream molecule. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Carboxylesterase 2 in the metabolic processing of these compounds, with Miconioside A possibly exerting its effects through a similar mechanism. The relationship is supported by the presence of multiple compounds with overlapping targets, suggesting a possible functional link between Miconioside A and Carboxylesterase 2 in the context of their biological activity.",
